Innovative Feature: IoT Mobile Key & Telematics Integration

To set this car rental system apart from traditional manual paperwork processes, the architecture
incorporates an "IoT Mobile Key Unlock" feature. Traditional rental agencies require customers to
physically visit a desk during business hours to retrieve keys, creating bottlenecks and limiting
operational hours. This enhancement integrates the rental software with IoT telematic devices 
installed in the fleet. Once an Admin changes a booking status to "Approved" in the system, a secure,
time-sensitive digital token is generated. This token would be transmitted to a companion mobile 
application, allowing the customer to unlock the car via Bluetooth or NFC directly from their smartphone.

Industry Requirement & Competitive Advantage:

This addresses a critical industry shift toward contactless, self-service rentals. It provides a severe
competitive advantage by enabling 24/7 vehicle dispatch without requiring round-the-clock on-site staffing.
Furthermore, because the Car class tracks precise variables like mileage and available_now, future
iterations of this IoT integration can automatically sync odometer readings back to the database at
the end of the rental period, completely automating the check-in and billing process.